==Serbo-Croatian==

===Alternative forms===
* (''Ijekavian''): {{l|sh|čȍvjek}}
* {{qualifier|Ikavian, Čakavian}}: {{l|sh|čovik}}, {{l|sh|človik}}
* {{qualifier|obsolete}}: {{l|sh|človek}}, {{l|sh|človjek}}

===Etymology===
From older {{term|človek|lang=sh}}, from {{etyl|sla-pro|sh}} {{term/t|sla-pro|*čьlověkъ}}, {{term/t|sla-pro|*čelověkъ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tʃôʋek/|lang=sh}}
* {{hyphenation|čo|vek}}

===Noun===
{{sh-noun|g=m|head=čȍvek|r|човек|чо̏век}}

# [[man]], [[person]]
#: {{usex|jeste li vidjeli ovog čov(j)eka?|t=have you seen this man?|lang=sh|inline=1}}
#: {{usex|ti si mrtav čov(j)ek|t=you're a dead man|lang=sh|inline=1}}
#: {{usex|zanemarite čov(j)eka iza zav(j)ese|t=pay no attention to the man behind the curtain|lang=sh|inline=1}}
# [[human]]
#: {{usex|ne želim biti čov(j)ek, želim biti robot!|t=I don't want to be human, I want to be a robot!|lang=sh|inline=1}}
#: {{usex|nisi zao, samo si...čov(j)ek|t=you're not evil, you're just...human|lang=sh|inline=1}}

